WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.624
Kits, sets, suggestions and side by side comparison make a bigger basket and an easier choice.

00:00:07.624 --> 00:00:12.659
This video shows how to sell a bundle, group products, add upsells and

00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:16.170
cross-sells, and let shoppers compare products.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.477
A shop sells more when shoppers see what goes together.

00:00:24.477 --> 00:00:28.670
A kit, a set and a few good suggestions make the basket bigger.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.910
Shoppers also choose faster when they can put products side by side.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.293
And stock stays right:

00:00:36.293 --> 00:00:40.025
a kit sells its parts, so the parts are counted, and a kit

00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:42.940
never promises more than the parts can make.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.870
Each of these is a separate feature that you turn on only when you need it.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.197
A bundle is several products sold as one product, at its own price,

00:00:56.197 --> 00:00:57.780
such as a starter kit.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:03.343
A grouped product shows several products on one page, each with a quantity,

00:01:03.343 --> 00:01:06.790
and one Add to cart adds the ones the shopper chose.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.123
Upsells are better or bigger choices.

00:01:10.123 --> 00:01:13.366
Cross-sells are things that go with the product.

00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:17.330
Related products and recently viewed products need no setup.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:21.100
Compare sets up to four products side by side.

00:01:25.287 --> 00:01:28.539
Create a product, and look for the Bundle section.

00:01:28.539 --> 00:01:31.907
Under Made of, choose the products the bundle holds.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:38.384
Search for a product by name and choose it, then say how many each bundle holds.

00:01:38.384 --> 00:01:42.798
This kit holds two ceramic mugs and a hardcover notebook.

00:01:50.964 --> 00:01:53.628
Give the kit a title and its own price.

00:01:53.628 --> 00:01:58.304
The price is what the shopper pays, whatever the parts cost on their own.

00:01:58.756 --> 00:02:00.965
Do not count the kit's own stock.

00:02:00.965 --> 00:02:06.006
Its stock is worked out from its parts, so leave Count stock unticked, and publish.

00:02:06.457 --> 00:02:10.363
On the shop, the kit shows Only 2 left, because four mugs make

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.177
two kits, and its page lists what is in it.

00:02:15.327 --> 00:02:20.148
Selling a kit takes each part from stock, and canceling or refunding the

00:02:20.148 --> 00:02:21.817
order puts them back.

00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:24.907
In Inventory, the mugs are counted as usual.

00:02:29.099 --> 00:02:33.369
For a set, use the Grouped products section on a new product.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:37.338
Under Products in this group, choose the products.

00:02:37.338 --> 00:02:40.919
This set has a lamp, a notebook and a water bottle.

00:02:53.844 --> 00:02:55.464
Give the set a title.

00:02:55.464 --> 00:02:59.304
It has no price of its own, and no stock to count, because

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:01.944
the products in it are what is bought.

00:03:01.944 --> 00:03:03.084
Then publish.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:08.886
The set's page lists each product with its price and stock, and a quantity for each.

00:03:08.886 --> 00:03:13.400
The shopper types how many of each, and one Add to cart adds them all.

00:03:17.669 --> 00:03:25.249
With Product Recommendations on, a product's editor has a Recommendations section, with Upsells and Cross-sells.

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:28.379
Upsells are better or bigger choices.

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:31.739
Cross-sells are things that go with the product.

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:36.218
For the ceramic mug, the water bottle is an upsell, and a notebook

00:03:36.218 --> 00:03:38.271
and a lamp are cross-sells.

00:03:38.271 --> 00:03:39.454
Then publish.

00:03:50.122 --> 00:03:53.862
The mug's page shows the upsell under You may also like.

00:03:58.295 --> 00:04:03.204
Below it, Recently viewed shows the products the shopper looked at before, kept

00:04:03.204 --> 00:04:04.764
in their own browser.

00:04:04.764 --> 00:04:10.365
Related products, from the product's categories, show the same way, when it has categories.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:16.557
In the cart, the cross-sells show as Frequently bought together, a click from the order.

00:04:20.758 --> 00:04:26.278
With Product Comparison on, each card and product page has a Compare tick box.

00:04:26.728 --> 00:04:30.344
A shopper ticks up to four products, and a bar at the bottom

00:04:30.344 --> 00:04:31.988
of the page counts them.

00:04:33.484 --> 00:04:37.987
Compare opens a page that sets them side by side, with the prices

00:04:37.987 --> 00:04:42.744
and stock, and a row for each specification, so the differences show.

00:04:46.944 --> 00:04:48.211
A starter kit:

00:04:48.211 --> 00:04:51.124
a bundle of a few products at one price.

00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:53.634
A matching collection:

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:57.154
a grouped product, with a quantity for each piece.

00:04:57.904 --> 00:04:59.283
A bigger basket:

00:04:59.283 --> 00:05:01.164
cross-sells in the cart.

00:05:01.914 --> 00:05:03.265
A hard choice:

00:05:03.265 --> 00:05:06.574
compare, with a row for each specification.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:12.102
A bundle, a group, suggestions and compare.

00:05:12.102 --> 00:05:13.974
Thanks for watching.

